<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">When Jamie Carragher appeared as a pundit =
on Sky Sports Super Sunday, Football Daily was surprised he didn=E2=80=99t =
have a solicitor sitting alongside him, occasionally jotting notes on a pad=
 or leaning over to give whispered instructions and answer =E2=80=9Cno comm=
ent=E2=80=9D to any leading questions about Trey Nyoni starting ahead of Ry=
an Gravenberch. On Friday night, the former Liverpool defender was subjecte=
d to a threat of legal action from Aston Villa, who took such grave excepti=
on to some =E2=80=9Cunacceptable insults=E2=80=9D he had rained down on the=
m from his podcast pulpit, that they were <a href=3D"https://ablink.editori=
al.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtj=
hYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgTuibY6nsmBnuxMdDsmcWmaXFEDi_kchJj87Ru25HRDREpT_K_gEVFqIGB=
UihytFHjKd_J5PF5h4yvwggGkqkQYcSWaCwJ0umx-ymjdcLUVWEALxlxYUBN_6Q5pC6LvYeqFe_=
CeQAaYV5XfOxxwlHFOYKvG63Gyyr-9jCNQuTwMBJ9oEMCxPjoZUJb1ipeFx2e5ELmvSiJdSClx2=
QtL4QYrXh_AAEB10kyAV7_6vfFA2PiN2jbj75TdIsVlfdd6JRC6i_YfUiCYTRsa-ZIPaWiA/4ve=
/0FD4L6e_T3mX59uU0fDAGg/h28/h001.DxRlcEvfWEGFGEhFdtrYDBYWcpgpyFjvHVkUwB00qz=
A" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">ready to call in the heavy legal artillery</a>=
 and stop him from preventing their =E2=80=9Cascension in English and Europ=
ean football=E2=80=9D. Taking a leaf out of the tried-and-much-ridiculed <a=
 href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_=
XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgkOliMzTbJaA7am0FSte37Lr3Co=
ZHvRoTi9n5wBtdZRg9iyH0wq7Xy4nD7Oa2Vqo8kAEdDPxartubEQW3DrV_mC8_Pi36bwO6u_4wI=
-XA1v7OEeWMnR97cswVWRO6uNCV6dw4GN6xovD-XBAJZd5Qg5aBBcFpYjRGKtQQk6nMsqOXglfA=
vfnrYL0ote04l49jH4bpYuvNhsmOrznvzz9ml2tCdsArBPy5bTrU5Lt9m1qFijg3NGlKefjDA_j=
9_4KQ/4ve/0FD4L6e_T3mX59uU0fDAGg/h29/h001.CZ06qvXKdugEiPP8-wRoOXe8RQUlj3V2x=
OUBINW4-pc" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Nottingham Forest playbook</a>, Villa=
 chair Nassef Sawiris appears to have eschewed contacting Carragher through=
 the usual formal channels and instead cajoled some unfortunate junior comm=
s staffer to make the portentous announcement on their Social Media Disgrac=
es.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Villa=E2=80=99s threat came on the back of=
 some fairly obvious observations he made on Stick To Football, when he poi=
nted out that English football has a food-chain and despite their commendab=
le successes in recent seasons, Villa aren=E2=80=99t quite as high up it as=
 the richest man in Egypt might like to think. During a debate about the li=
kelihood of Unai Emery leaving Villa to take over the soon-to-be-vacant hea=
d coach=E2=80=99s job at Manchester United, Carragher had said the Spaniard=
 would =E2=80=9Cwant that opportunity to manage a giant again=E2=80=9D, bef=
ore pointing out =E2=80=9Cthere is a chain in football, whether you like it=
 or not=E2=80=9D. As controversial footballing takes go, it was right up th=
ere with pointing out that bears defecate in the woods and Pope Leo XIV wea=
rs a funny hat. =E2=80=9CSo shut the [eff] up Aston Villa fans,=E2=80=9D ho=
nked Carragher, hitting his stride. =E2=80=9CAston Villa will never be Manc=
hester United.=E2=80=9D</p>
