<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Of course, with this being football, there=
 is always a danger that explicitly signposted and totally anodyne badinage=
 will inevitably be misinterpreted by thin-skinned folk who are desperate t=
o be offended. But it is usually self-professed terminally-online superfans=
, not multi-billionaire club chairs whose hands instinctively reach for the=
ir pearls. While it remains unclear what exactly it was he said that was ac=
tionable, Carragher subsequently apologised for his comments. =E2=80=9CI=E2=
=80=99d like to apologise to Aston Villa, the owners &amp; their fans,=E2=
=80=9D he trumpeted from his soapbox in the digital town square. =E2=80=9CM=
y language this week was clumsy &amp; wrong. I can assure Villa fans it was=
 tongue in cheek but I can understand it=E2=80=99s not come across that way=
, so apologies. Good luck today UTV!=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It has now been widely reported that Villa=
 have dropped their threat of unspecified legal action against Carragher bu=
t it remains to be seen if Fulham can look forward to hearing from their la=
wyers after helping to prevent their ascension up the league after [Snip! S=
nip! Snippety-snip! =E2=80=93 Football Daily Lawyers] at Villa Park <a href=
=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18I=
RyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgxSVVLHYac7zt4a5YfhTAO_DYyps05kj=
